    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "buildTtdDb(): default rerun to FALSE, not TRUE\n\nEvery other download*()/build*() function in this package defaults to\nrerun=TRUE (check-for-updates-first), which is fine for functions no\none calls casually. buildTtdDb() is cheap (~5s once cached) and gets\ncalled bare routinely in its own Rd example, both test files' fixture\nhelpers, and (until recently) the vignette - each of those calls was\nsilently rebuilding and re-caching the database from scratch, since\nrerun=TRUE skips the \"reuse existing\" branch entirely. Traced this\nafter cleaning up 8 redundant cached copies of ttd_10.1.01.db that had\naccumulated from routine R CMD check / test runs this session.\n\nVerified: a bare buildTtdDb() call now completes in ~0.3s and reuses\nthe existing cache entry instead of rebuilding; all 83 ttdAccess/\ndrugTargetMeta tests still pass.\n",
    "time": 1784341134
  },
